Description: Secure network utilities using Magic Wormhole
 Critical Wormhole Tools (wh/cwt) provides secure network utilities
 using Magic Wormhole code-based addressing. Instead of IP addresses
 and port forwarding, users share human-readable codes like
 "7-guitar-sunset" to connect securely from anywhere.
 .
 Features include:
  - wh nc: Netcat-style bidirectional pipe
  - wh ssh: SSH client over wormhole
  - wh scp: Secure file copy
  - wh sftp: Interactive SFTP client
  - wh curl/wget: HTTP through wormhole
  - wh tunnel: Port forwarding
  - WNS: Wormhole Name Service for persistent addresses
